Use case: identity-preserve.
Asset type: production 2D desktop-pet animation source sheet. Exactly EIGHT sequential complete full-body poses of the ONE same character, arranged in FOUR equal columns and TWO equal rows, read left to right then next row. Each pose is separate with generous transparent gutters. No labels or grid lines.
Input image: authoritative identity reference of Guga, female Endministrator penguin onesie mascot, already approved by user. Preserve exact 2D anime linework, face shape, black bob haircut and straight bangs, blue-gray eyes with warm lower iris, silver black hairclip on viewer's left, charcoal hood with white oval eyes and yellow beak above forehead, white belly, red collar clasp and large single silver carabiner clasp, yellow webbed feet and short tail on viewer's right. SAME head/body proportions, not 3D, not realistic fur.
Action: IDLE breathing and blink loop. Keep both flippers naturally relaxed diagonally down at sides, do not hold the raised celebration pose in the reference. Round compact standing shape, head about half the total height. Gentle small smile, not permanently open shouting mouth.
Eight distinct hand-drawn key poses:
1 relaxed neutral, eyes open;
2 breathe in slightly, collar and belly rise subtly;
3 breath peak, upper eyelids relax;
4 eyes halfway closed beginning blink, body settles;
5 eyes closed in soft natural blink, body slightly lowers;
6 eyes halfway reopen, subtle return breathing;
7 eyes open, very slight curious head tilt;
8 return toward the neutral pose, eyes open.
Small continuous differences, relaxed and cute. Feet stay planted on exactly the same baseline within every cell, body scale identical. Do not move the whole character up and down to fake breathing.
Composition: equal-sized complete characters, each 82 percent or less of its slot height, all accessories and feet fully visible. True transparent alpha background. No floor, no shadow outside character, no checkerboard painted in, no border, no text, no watermarks, no effects. Exactly 4 columns x 2 rows, exactly 8 poses. No stray props, no human fingers, no new costume elements.
